# Who may approve an INFRASTRUCTURE change, and how many approvals one needs.
#
# Infrastructure means AltDigital's own layer: anything the platform builds,
# tagged platform-layer: infrastructure, deployed by a platform role and
# reconciled against AltDigital's ops project. Decided by Jamie, 2026-10-01:
#
#     Wayne, Art and Tina approve infrastructure changes; two approvals.
#
# The person who BUILDS the change does not appear here, so a requester cannot
# count towards their own approval. Change reconciliation also excludes the
# change record's reporter explicitly, in case the lists ever overlap.
#
# Application changes are NOT here. They belong to each tenant's own change
# process and records. For Arc8 those live in OEight's Jira, which the platform
# cannot read (see docs/deviations.md D-027).
#
# Atlassian accountIds, not email addresses: the accountId is what an approval
# record carries. Find one with scripts/jira-check.sh, or at
#   https://<site>.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/myself
#
# Copy this file to config/change-approvers.env and fill it in. That file is
# gitignored and blocked by the pre-commit hook: an accountId identifies a
# person. Publish with scripts/sync-change-approvers.sh.
INFRA_APPROVER_1=""      # Wayne
INFRA_APPROVER_2=""      # Art
INFRA_APPROVER_3=""      # Tina

# Distinct authorised approvals an infrastructure change needs. Two.
INFRA_MINIMUM_APPROVALS="2"
